{"data": {"box": "Ryzen 5 5500 (6C/12T), Windows 11, other builds and live music running concurrently: see machine_cpu_pct_during in each entry", "build": "release, opt-level 3, LTO off, 16 codegen units (tests/bench/run.sh)", "caveat": "latency numbers are timer/IO bound; CPU numbers are limited by the 15.6 ms process-time tick. Everything runs against a fake Spotify and a fake Discord pipe, never the real ones.", "date": "2026-10-05", "notes": ["a_track_change: the change now comes ~4 s after the previous one (quiet) because the settle depends on whether another change happened in the last 3 s; the old ~2 s spacing is the entry ending in _2s_after_previous_change.", "The bridge JS used by js_e2e / js_lyrics_hang is the new 2.2 file; with the old JS the song-change/pause reaction and the 5 s lyric timeout do not apply.", "In e_bridge_ws_drop, engine_still_reports_bridge_connected_after_silence is false because a peer that never speaks is not counted as the bridge. A null drop_to_presence_cleared_ms with clears_sent_by_the_blip 0 means the blip was shorter than the pause hold and the profile was left alone.", "i_discord_hangup: with a hang-up 150 ms or 450 ms after READY nothing can be shown at all (the first frame waits 400 ms); those rows have no frames and prove nothing about the budget. The 600 ms, 1 s and 2 s rows do.", "seek_event_to_engine is the 500 ms poll's random phase, unchanged by the work: with 8 trials its median moved between runs (171, 311, 313 ms), with 24 trials per side (js_e2e_24_trials.jsonl) the means are 259 ms before and 248 ms after."], "what": "AFTER the perf/bridge changes, final code of the branch (the commit that contains this file), same harness and method as baseline.jsonl; BENCH_JS_TRIALS=8. New since the earlier AFTER file (3630607): h_pause_flapping, i_discord_hangup, j_bridge_flap (the rate budget under pause/resume flapping, a Discord that hangs up after READY, and a bridge socket that keeps dropping), and the pause hold (presence::PAUSE_HOLD, 1.5 s): pause_to_clear and pause_event_to_clear are therefore ~1.6 s, where the baseline (master) cleared within ~50 ms (UI-less) / ~200 ms (through the real bridge JS) but without counting the clear against Discord's 5-per-20-s budget. e_bridge_ws_drop was re-run on its own after adding the clears_sent_by_the_blip field (same code). The baseline file is the earlier session's run of master + harness (4a6266a); baseline-session.jsonl (not in this file) is a re-run of the same harness on master in the same session as this file, for the cases the README quotes."}, "name": "_meta"}

